# Revisions listed here are skipped by `git blame`.
#
# Only add commits that are purely mechanical (formatters, licence headers,
# whitespace) and provably contain no behavioural change. Never add a commit
# that mixes formatting with real edits -- blame would then hide real authorship.
#
# Enable locally with:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub applies this file automatically in its blame view.
#
# MAINTAINERS: this repository squash-merges, so the SHA of a formatting commit
# inside a pull request never reaches `main` and cannot be listed here in advance.
# A squash also collapses every commit in a PR into one, so the SHA is only safe
# to list if that PR contained *nothing but* the reformat. A PR that mixes the
# reformat with configuration or documentation changes produces a squash commit
# that is not purely mechanical, and listing it would hide real authorship.
#
# So the reformat has to land as its own pull request. After squash-merging it,
# append the squashed SHA (`git log -1 --format=%H` on `main`) below with a
# one-line description. Git silently ignores entries that do not resolve to a
# real commit, so an unfilled placeholder fails *open*: blame keeps attributing
# reformatted lines to the formatting commit, with nothing to indicate the entry
# is dead.
# See CONTRIBUTING.md ("`git blame` and the formatting commit") for context.

